#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr ""
"Un curso gratuito de IBM sobre información cuántica y computación cuántica"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems and reduced states"
msgstr "Sistemas múltiples y estados reducidos"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll turn our attention to how density matrices work for multiple "
"systems, including examples of different types of correlations they can "
"express and how they can be used to describe the states of isolated parts of"
" compound systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora nos dirigimos a la cuestión de cómo funcionan las matrices de densidad"
" para sistemas múltiples — incluyendo ejemplos de diferentes tipos de "
"correlaciones que pueden expresar, y cómo pueden usarse para describir los "
"estados de partes aisladas de sistemas compuestos.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems {#multiple-systems}"
msgstr "Sistemas múltiples {#multiple-systems}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices can represent states of multiple systems in an analogous way to state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information, following the same basic idea that multiple systems can be viewed as if they're single, compound systems.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the rows and columns of density matrices representing states of multiple systems are placed in correspondence with the Cartesian product of the classical state sets of the individual systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las matrices de densidad pueden representar estados de sistemas múltiples de manera análoga a los vectores de estado en la formulación simplificada de la información cuántica, donde se aplica la misma idea básica: sistemas múltiples pueden considerarse como si fueran un único sistema compuesto.\n"
"Matemáticamente, las filas y columnas de las matrices de densidad que representan estados de sistemas múltiples corresponden al producto cartesiano de los conjuntos de estados clásicos de los sistemas individuales.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, recall the state vector representations of the four Bell "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Recordemos, por ejemplo, las representaciones como vectores de estado de los"
" cuatro estados de Bell.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representations of these states are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las representaciones como matrices de densidad de estos estados son las "
"siguientes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Product states {#product-states}"
msgstr "Estados producto {#product-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we had for state vectors, tensor products of density matrices represent *independence* between the states of multiple systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ is prepared in the state represented by the density matrix $\\rho$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ is independently prepared in the state represented by $\\sigma,$ then the density matrix describing the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is the tensor product $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"De manera similar a los vectores de estado, los productos tensoriales de matrices de densidad representan *independencia* entre los estados de sistemas múltiples.\n"
"Si, por ejemplo, $\\mathsf{X}$ se prepara en el estado dado por la matriz de densidad $\\rho$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ se prepara independientemente en el estado $\\sigma,$ entonces la matriz de densidad que describe el estado de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ es el producto tensorial $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same terminology is used here as in the simplified formulation of "
"quantum information: states of this form are referred to as *product "
"states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Se utiliza la misma terminología que en la formulación simplificada de la "
"información cuántica: los estados de esta forma se denominan *estados "
"producto*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correlated and entangled states {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"
msgstr ""
"Estados correlacionados y entrelazados {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States that cannot be expressed as product states represent *correlations* between systems.\n"
"There are, in fact, different types of correlations that can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Here are a few examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Los estados que no pueden expresarse como estados producto representan *correlaciones* entre sistemas.\n"
"De hecho, existen diferentes tipos de correlaciones que pueden representarse mediante matrices de densidad.\n"
"Aquí hay algunos ejemplos.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Correlated classical states.*\n"
"For example, we can express the situation in which Alice and Bob share a random bit like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Estados clásicos correlacionados.*\n"
"Por ejemplo, podemos expresar la situación en la que Alice y Bob comparten un bit aleatorio de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Ensembles of quantum states.*\n"
"Suppose we have $m$ density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ all representing states of a system $\\mathsf{X},$ and we  randomly choose one of these states according to a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Such a process is represented by an *ensemble* of states, which includes the specification of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ as well as the probabilities $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ We can associate an ensemble of states with a single density matrix, describing both the random choice of $k$ and the corresponding density matrix $\\rho_k,$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ensambles de estados cuánticos.*\n"
"Supongamos que tenemos $m$ matrices de densidad $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ todas representando estados de un sistema $\\mathsf{X},$ y elegimos uno de estos estados aleatoriamente según un vector de probabilidad $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Un proceso así se representa mediante un *ensamble* de estados, que incluye la especificación de las matrices de densidad $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1}$ así como las probabilidades $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Podemos asociar a un ensamble de estados una única matriz de densidad que describe tanto la elección aleatoria de $k$ como la correspondiente matriz de densidad $\\rho_k,$ de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To be clear, this is the state of a pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ "
"where $\\mathsf{Y}$ represents the classical selection of $k$ — so we're "
"assuming its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ States of this "
"form are sometimes called *classical-quantum states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para ser claros: este es el estado de un par $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}),$"
" donde $\\mathsf{Y}$ representa la selección clásica de $k$ — por lo que "
"asumimos que su conjunto de estados clásicos es $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ Los "
"estados de esta forma se denominan a veces *estados clásico-cuánticos*.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Separable states*. We can imagine situations in which we have a classical "
"correlation among the quantum states of two systems like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Estados separables*. Podemos imaginar situaciones en las que tenemos una "
"correlación clásica entre los estados cuánticos de dos sistemas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In words, for each $k$ from $0$ to $m-1,$ we have that with probability "
"$p_k$ the system on the left is in the state $\\rho_k$ and the system on the"
" right is in the state $\\sigma_k.$ States like this are called *separable "
"states*. This concept can also be extended to more than two systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dicho de otra forma: para cada $k$ de $0$ a $m-1,$ con probabilidad "
"$p_k,$ el sistema izquierdo está en el estado $\\rho_k$ y el sistema derecho"
" en el estado $\\sigma_k.$ Los estados de esta forma se denominan *estados "
"separables*. Este concepto también se extiende a más de dos sistemas.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entangled states*. Not all states of pairs of systems are separable. In the"
" general formulation of quantum information, this is how entanglement is "
"defined: states that are not separable are said to be *entangled*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Estados entrelazados*. No todos los estados de pares de sistemas son "
"separables. En la formulación general de la información cuántica, el "
"entrelazamiento se define exactamente de esta manera: los estados que no son"
" separables se denominan *entrelazados*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that this terminology is consistent with the terminology we used in "
"the \"Basics of quantum information\" course. There we said that quantum "
"state vectors that are not product states represent entangled states — and "
"indeed, for any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that is not a "
"product state, we find that the state represented by the density matrix "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is not separable. Entanglement is "
"much more complicated than this for states that are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Esta terminología es consistente con la del curso \"Fundamentos de la "
"información cuántica\". Allí dijimos que los vectores de estado cuántico que"
" no son estados producto representan estados entrelazados — y de hecho, para"
" cualquier vector de estado cuántico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ que no sea un "
"estado producto, el estado representado por la matriz de densidad "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ no es separable. Sin embargo, para "
"estados que no son puros, el entrelazamiento es considerablemente más "
"complicado.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states and the partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Estados reducidos y la traza parcial {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a simple but important thing we can do with density matrices in the context of multiple systems, which is to describe the states we obtain by ignoring some of the systems.\n"
"When multiple systems are in a quantum state and we discard or choose to ignore one or more of the systems,\n"
"the state of the remaining systems is called the *reduced state* of those systems.\n"
"Density matrix descriptions of reduced states are easily obtained through a mapping, known as the *partial trace*, from the density matrix describing the state of the whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"En el contexto de sistemas múltiples, hay una operación simple pero importante que podemos realizar con matrices de densidad: describir los estados que obtenemos cuando ignoramos algunos de los sistemas.\n"
"Cuando varios sistemas se encuentran juntos en un estado cuántico y descartamos o ignoramos uno o más sistemas, el estado de los sistemas restantes se denomina el *estado reducido* de esos sistemas.\n"
"Las descripciones como matrices de densidad de los estados reducidos pueden obtenerse fácilmente a partir de la matriz de densidad del sistema completo mediante una aplicación conocida como la *traza parcial*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: reduced states for an e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo: estados reducidos para un e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-"
"bit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ that are "
"together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que tenemos un par de qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ que se "
"encuentran juntos en el estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can imagine that Alice holds the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ and Bob holds $\\mathsf{B},$ which is to say that together they share an e-bit.\n"
"We'd like to have a density matrix description of Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, as if Bob decided to take his qubit and visit the stars, never to be seen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Imaginemos que Alice posee el qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ y Bob posee el qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ — juntos comparten un e-bit.\n"
"Queremos obtener una descripción como matriz de densidad del qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ de Alice en aislamiento, como si Bob hubiera decidido tomar su qubit y viajar a las estrellas para nunca más ser visto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First let's think about what would happen if Bob decided somewhere on his journey to measure his qubit with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"If he did this, he would obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Pensemos primero en lo que pasaría si Bob decidiera, en algún punto de su viaje, medir su qubit en una medición de base estándar.\n"
"Si lo hiciera, obtendría el resultado $0$ con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ and he "
"would obtain the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"donde el estado del qubit de Alice se convierte en $\\vert 0\\rangle$; y "
"obtendría el resultado $1$ con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "donde el estado del qubit de Alice se convierte en $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we ignore Bob's measurement outcome and focus on Alice's qubit, we conclude that she obtains the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with probability $1/2.$\n"
"This leads us to describe the state of Alice's qubit in isolation by the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Si ignoramos el resultado de la medición de Bob y nos concentramos en el qubit de Alice, concluimos que ella obtiene el estado $\\vert 0\\rangle$ con probabilidad $1/2$ y el estado $\\vert 1\\rangle$ con probabilidad $1/2.$\n"
"Esto nos lleva a describir el estado del qubit de Alice en aislamiento mediante la matriz de densidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, Alice's qubit is in the completely mixed state.\n"
"To be clear, this description of the state of Alice's qubit doesn't include Bob's measurement outcome; we're ignoring Bob altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"Es decir, el qubit de Alice se encuentra en el estado completamente mezclado.\n"
"Para ser claros: esta descripción del estado del qubit de Alice no incluye el resultado de la medición de Bob; ignoramos a Bob por completo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it might seem like the density matrix description of Alice's qubit in isolation that we've just obtained relies on the assumption that Bob has measured his qubit, but this is not actually so.\n"
"What we've done is to use the possibility that Bob measures his qubit to argue that the completely mixed state arises as the state of Alice's qubit, based on what we've already learned.\n"
"Of course, nothing says that Bob must measure his qubit — but nothing says that he doesn't.\n"
"And if he's light years away, then nothing he does or doesn't do can possibly influence the state of Alice's qubit viewed it in isolation.\n"
"That is to say, the description we've obtained for the state of Alice's qubit is the only description consistent with the impossibility of faster-than-light communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Puede parecer que la descripción como matriz de densidad del qubit de Alice en aislamiento obtenida depende de la suposición de que Bob midió su qubit, pero en realidad no es así.\n"
"Lo que hicimos fue usar la posibilidad de que Bob mida su qubit para argumentar que el estado completamente mezclado surge como estado del qubit de Alice, basándonos en lo que ya habíamos aprendido.\n"
"Por supuesto, nada dice que Bob deba medir su qubit — pero tampoco nada dice que no lo haga.\n"
"Y si está a años luz de distancia, nada de lo que haga o deje de hacer puede afectar posiblemente al estado del qubit de Alice en aislamiento.\n"
"Es decir, la descripción que obtuvimos para el estado del qubit de Alice es la única descripción compatible con la imposibilidad de la comunicación superlumínica.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider the state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ which happens to be the completely mixed state as well.\n"
"Indeed, for all four Bell states we find that the reduced state of both Alice's qubit and Bob's qubit is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"También podemos considerar el estado del qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ de Bob, que igualmente es el estado completamente mezclado.\n"
"Para los cuatro estados de Bell, el estado reducido tanto del qubit de Alice como del de Bob es el estado completamente mezclado.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states for a general quantum state vector {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"
msgstr ""
"Estados reducidos para un vector de estado cuántico general {#reduced-"
"states-for-a-general-quantum-state-vector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's generalize the example just discussed to two arbitrary systems $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ not necessarily qubits in the state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"We'll assume the classical state sets of $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are $\\Sigma$ and $\\Gamma,$ respectively.\n"
"A density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the combined system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ therefore has row and column indices corresponding to the Cartesian product $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Generalicemos ahora el ejemplo que acabamos de discutir a dos sistemas arbitrarios $\\mathsf{A}$ y $\\mathsf{B},$ que no necesariamente son qubits en el estado $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Asumimos que los conjuntos de estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{A}$ y $\\mathsf{B}$ son $\\Sigma$ y $\\Gamma$ respectivamente.\n"
"Una matriz de densidad $\\rho$ que representa un estado del sistema combinado $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ tiene, por tanto, índices de fila y columna que corresponden al producto cartesiano $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that the state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is described by the quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ so the density matrix describing this state is $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"We'll obtain a density matrix description of the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, which is conventionally denoted $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A superscript is also sometimes used rather than a subscript.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que el estado de $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ se describe por el vector de estado cuántico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ de modo que la matriz de densidad que describe este estado es $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"Determinamos una descripción como matriz de densidad del estado de $\\mathsf{A}$ en aislamiento, que habitualmente se denota $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A veces se usa un superíndice en lugar de un subíndice.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the form\n"
msgstr "El vector de estado $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ puede expresarse en la forma\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a uniquely determined collection of vectors $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"In particular, these vectors can be determined through a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"para una colección de vectores $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}$ unívocamente determinada.\n"
"Estos vectores pueden determinarse, en particular, mediante una fórmula sencilla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reasoning similarly to the previous example of an e-bit, if we were to "
"measure the system $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement, we would"
" obtain each outcome $b\\in\\Gamma$ with probability "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ in which case the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"De manera análoga al ejemplo anterior del e-bit: si midiéramos el sistema "
"$\\mathsf{B}$ con una medición de base estándar, obtendríamos cada resultado"
" $b\\in\\Gamma$ con probabilidad $\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ y el "
"estado de $\\mathsf{A}$ se convertiría entonces en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As a density matrix, this state can be written as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como matriz de densidad, este estado puede escribirse de la siguiente "
"manera.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Averaging the different states according to the probabilities of the "
"respective outcomes, we arrive at the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Promediando los diferentes estados según las probabilidades de los "
"respectivos resultados, llegamos a la matriz de densidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "La traza parcial {#the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The formula\n"
msgstr "La fórmula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"leads us to the description of the reduced state of $\\mathsf{A}$ for any "
"density matrix $\\rho$ of the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ not just a "
"pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"nos lleva a la descripción del estado reducido de $\\mathsf{A}$ para "
"cualquier matriz de densidad $\\rho$ del par $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ no"
" solo para un estado puro.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula must work, simply by linearity together with the fact that "
"every density matrix can be written as a convex combination of pure "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta fórmula debe cumplirse, simplemente por linealidad junto con el hecho "
"de que toda matriz de densidad puede escribirse como combinación convexa de "
"estados puros.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation being performed on $\\rho$ to obtain $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ in this equation is known as the *partial trace*, and to be more precise we say that the partial trace is performed on $\\mathsf{B},$ or that $\\mathsf{B}$ is *traced out*.\n"
"This operation is denoted $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ so we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"La operación que se realiza sobre $\\rho$ para obtener $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ se denomina *traza parcial*, y más concretamente decimos que la traza parcial se realiza sobre $\\mathsf{B}$ o que $\\mathsf{B}$ se *traza fuera*.\n"
"Esta operación se denota $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ de modo que podemos escribir\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define the partial trace on $\\mathsf{A},$ so it's the system "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ that gets traced out rather than $\\mathsf{B},$ like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"También podemos definir la traza parcial sobre $\\mathsf{A},$ de modo que el"
" sistema $\\mathsf{A}$ se traza fuera en lugar de $\\mathsf{B},$ de la "
"siguiente manera.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives us the density matrix description $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ of the "
"state of $\\mathsf{B}$ in isolation rather than $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto nos da la descripción como matriz de densidad $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ del"
" estado de $\\mathsf{B}$ en aislamiento en lugar de $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recapitulate, if $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is any pair of systems and "
"we have a density matrix $\\rho$ describing a state of "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ the *reduced states* of the systems "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"En resumen: si $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ es un par de sistemas cualquiera "
"y tenemos una matriz de densidad $\\rho$ que describe un estado de "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ los *estados reducidos* de los sistemas "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ y $\\mathsf{B}$ son los siguientes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho$ is a density matrix, then $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ will also necessarily be density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si $\\rho$ es una matriz de densidad, $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ y "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ son necesariamente también matrices de densidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These notions can be generalized to any number of systems in place of two in a natural way.\n"
"In general, we can put the names of whatever systems we choose in the subscript of a density matrix $\\rho$ to describe the reduced state of just those systems.\n"
"For example, if $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ and $\\mathsf{C}$ are systems and $\\rho$ is a density matrix describing a state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ then we can define\n"
msgstr ""
"Estos conceptos se generalizan de manera natural a un número arbitrario de sistemas en lugar de dos.\n"
"En general, podemos indicar los nombres de cualesquiera sistemas en el subindice de una matriz de densidad $\\rho$ para describir el estado reducido de exactamente esos sistemas.\n"
"Si $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B}$ y $\\mathsf{C}$ son, por ejemplo, sistemas y $\\rho$ es una matriz de densidad que describe un estado de $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ entonces podemos definir:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and similarly for other choices for the systems.\n"
msgstr "y de forma correspondiente para otras selecciones de sistemas.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Descripción alternativa de la traza parcial {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to describe the partial trace mappings "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ is"
" that they are the *unique* linear mappings that satisfy the formulas\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma alternativa de describir las aplicaciones de traza parcial "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ y $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ es "
"que son las *únicas* aplicaciones lineales que satisfacen las fórmulas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these formulas, $N$ and $M$ are square matrices of the appropriate sizes:\n"
"the rows and columns of $M$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{A}$ and the rows and columns of $N$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"En estas fórmulas, $N$ y $M$ son matrices cuadradas de tamaño adecuado:\n"
"las filas y columnas de $M$ corresponden a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{A}$ y las filas y columnas de $N$ corresponden a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This characterization of the partial trace is not only fundamental from a mathematical viewpoint, but can also allow for quick calculations in some situations.\n"
"For example, consider this state of a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta caracterización de la traza parcial no solo es fundamental desde un punto de vista matemático, sino que también permite cálculos rápidos en algunas situaciones.\n"
"Consideremos, por ejemplo, el siguiente estado de un par de qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute the reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ for instance, we can use linearity together with the fact that\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ and $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ have unit trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para calcular el estado reducido $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}},$ podemos usar la linealidad junto con el hecho de que\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ y $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ tienen traza unitaria.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ can be computed similarly.\n"
msgstr "El estado reducido $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ se calcula de manera similar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"
msgstr "La traza parcial para dos qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partial trace can also be described explicitly in terms of matrices.\n"
"Here we'll do this just for two qubits, but this can also be generalized to larger systems.\n"
"Assume that we have two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ so that any density matrix describing a state of these two qubits can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"La traza parcial también puede describirse explícitamente en términos de matrices.\n"
"Lo hacemos aquí solo para dos qubits, pero esto puede generalizarse a sistemas más grandes.\n"
"Supongamos que tenemos dos qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ de modo que cualquier matriz de densidad que describa un estado de estos dos qubits puede escribirse como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some choice of complex numbers $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para una elección de números complejos $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq "
"3\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace over the first system has the following formula.\n"
msgstr "La traza parcial sobre el primer sistema tiene la siguiente fórmula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to think about this formula begins by viewing $4\\times 4$ matrices as $2\\times 2$ block matrices, where each block is $2\\times 2.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma de entender esta fórmula es considerar las matrices $4\\times 4$ como matrices de bloques $2\\times 2,$ donde cada bloque es $2\\times 2.$\n"
"Es decir,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "para\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then have\n"
msgstr "Entonces\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the formula when the second system is traced out rather than the "
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí está la fórmula cuando se traza fuera el segundo sistema en lugar del "
"primero.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In terms of block matrices of a form similar to before, we have this "
"formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"En términos de matrices de bloques de forma similar a la anterior, se tiene "
"la siguiente fórmula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The block matrix descriptions of these functions can be extended to systems "
"larger than qubits in a natural and direct way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las descripciones en términos de matrices de bloques de estas funciones se "
"generalizan de manera natural y directa a sistemas más grandes que qubits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To finish the lesson, let's apply these formulas to the same state we "
"considered above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para concluir la lección, aplicamos estas fórmulas al mismo estado que "
"consideramos antes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state of the first system $\\mathsf{A}$ is\n"
msgstr "El estado reducido del primer sistema $\\mathsf{A}$ es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the reduced state of the second system $\\mathsf{B}$ is\n"
msgstr "y el estado reducido del segundo sistema $\\mathsf{B}$ es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
